            <ArticleTitle>Right coronary ostial aneurysm following a bentall procedure.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>632-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1540-8191.2011.01319.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of a 69-year-old female with a previous Bentall procedure who developed a right coronary ostial aneurysm. The aneurysm was excluded with a Dacron patch and the right internal mammary artery was used to restore flow to the coronary artery.</AbstractText>
